cff-version: 1.0.0
message: "If you use zh-emotion in your research, please cite this repository."
title: "zh-emotion: Context-Aware Emotion Analysis for Chinese Text"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - Chinese language
  - emotion analysis
  - contextual interpretation
  - conversational analysis
  - literary analysis
  - large language models
  - agent skills
abstract: >
  An LLM skill for analyzing emotions in Chinese-language sentences,
  conversations, literary works, and other textual contexts. It uses a
  technique-content-effect-emotion framework to organize interpretations,
  identify emotional subjects and targets, trace contextual shifts, and
  distinguish explicit statements from inferences. Outputs preserve textual
  evidence, alternative interpretations, and uncertainty, with optional
  structured formats for downstream models and agents.
authors:
